WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Good morning John, it's January 20th.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:03.820
Henry Green's birthday.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.480
Can we, uh, cue the epic music?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.120
(Epic music)

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.380
In 1995, John Green was a senior in high school.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.640
He was so cool that he took little notice

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.400
of a young freshman named Sarah. In fact, asked about it years later,

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.340
John Green says, "Well, I think I thought she was kind of cute."

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.280
Sarah, on the other hand, quite clearly remembers the charmingly nerdy

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.360
upperclassman, though their interactions were few.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.440
After graduation, 10 years had to pass before their paths would cross again.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.160
In a peculiar turn of events, Sarah was punching John Green's ex-girlfriend in the face one day,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.980
when it came out that she was, in fact, from Alabama. The two were sparring partners at a Chicago

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:58.200
boxing club. And John's ex-girlfriend said, "my ex-boyfriend is also from Alabama."

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:04.860
Though she probably didn't say it quite like that. Slowly it came out that the ex-boyfriend of the sparring partner

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.920
was in fact that charmingly nerdy upperclassman, John Green.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.480
Thus, reconnected by the sparring partner and ex-girlfriend, John and Sarah began a string of emails

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.880
that stretched over a year in time and became roughly the length of a short Russian novel.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.440
These collected emails have since been the subject of intense study

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.900
from scholars in the field of technology-based literature to scholars in the field of true love.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.380
And they led, eventually, to a string of dates in 2004.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:45.120
In 2005, Sarah arrived home to find a single red rose placed on every step rising to her 4th floor apartement.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:49.480
And at the top, waiting for her, was John Green carrying more roses

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.060
and a ring.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:57.380
The couple were married in a beautiful, traditional ceremony in a large Alabama church.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:01.020
They then lived together happily for years with their puppy

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.060
Fireball Wilson 'Willie' Roberts.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:12.560
It wasn't until early 2010, earlier today in fact, that John and Sarah's two became three,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.320
when Henry Green was born.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:21.660
We can only assume that Henry was named after John's younger, smarter, better looking brother.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:27.720
Or possibly after his grandfather. Though it is clear from the mass of black hair on his head

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.300
that he will take after his mother, for which we are all intensly greatful.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.140
Henry Green was born early in the morning of January 20th.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.360
The event was described by John as "freaking weird, man!"

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:46.420
And then later as, "She just worked so hard, and now there's, like, this... person, like, a PERSON!"

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.580
John described the feeling of fatherhood as, "Actually, like, really great."

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.220
and continued to point out that "I don't even really know what's going on, man,

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.940
I've been awake for 46 of the last 48 hours."

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.360
John, Sarah, and Henry are now enjoying some much deserved rest,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.660
and we would like to remind everyone that John's baby needs gifts.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.820
So please follow the link in the sidebar to give John Green's baby the only gift he wants:

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.100
a world without malaria.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:21.500
John Green's paternity leave thus begun. Maureen Johnson, I will see you on Friday.

